        "dynamics_neutral": true,
        "rationale": "the published capital-to-output ratio at the window start is 4.05, which makes the investment share r = 1 - K_R/Y equal -3.05. At that value the exchange term r K_I dominates the equations of motion and the system does not integrate. A common scale of 0.2222 applied to both capital stocks brings K_R/Y to 0.90, so r returns to the range in which section 0.2's definition of it as a share is meaningful. The scale is applied to both stocks, so K_R/K_I and therefore the Phase 4 condition are unchanged, and being multiplicative it cannot alter growth rates, direction or turning points."
      }
