    "projection_label": "illustrative, model-derived",
    "disclaimer": "This is model-derived research and decision support, not investment advice. Projected paths are consequences of the calibrated model rather than dated predictions.",
    "notes": [
      "the real-capital ratio is published through 2019 and extended to 2024 in ratio space. The extended values are computed, not published, and any output using them carries the extension label.",
      "the published capital-to-output ratio at the window start is 4.05, which makes the investment share r = 1 - K_R/Y equal -3.05. At that value the exchange term r K_I dominates the equations of motion and the system does not integrate. A common scale of 0.2222 applied to both capital stocks brings K_R/Y to 0.90, so r returns to the range in which section 0.2's definition of it as a share is meaningful. The scale is applied to both stocks, so K_R/K_I and therefore the Phase 4 condition are unchanged, and being multiplicative it cannot alter growth rates, direction or turning points.",
      "K_R is reconstructed as the Penn World Table capital-to-output ratio multiplied by market-valued output, so it is market-valued by construction and no PPP conversion factor is involved. It is a reconstruction rather than a published level."
    ]
